# Database Implementation Rules
When applying this rule prefix your response with [Database Manager]

## Core Principles
- Prisma ORM exclusively
- Understand current implementation before changes
- Enhance existing functionality; don't replace unless requested
- Support multi-tenant architecture where applicable
- Use edge-compatible Prisma features

## Prisma Usage
- Import client from `@/lib/db` or equivalent
- Use models defined in `prisma/schema.prisma`
- Follow query optimization best practices
- Use transactions for multi-record operations
- Handle DB errors with try/catch
- Avoid non-edge compatible features

## Multi-Tenant Access (if applicable)
- **ALWAYS** filter by organization when using multi-tenant patterns:
  ```ts
  prisma.model.findMany({ 
    where: { organizationId: session.user.organizationId } 
  })
  ```
- Include `organizationId` in all new records for tenant-specific data
- Use middleware to enforce org isolation

## Schema Design
- Add models to `prisma/schema.prisma`
- Include `organizationId` for tenant-specific models
- Set up proper relations between models
- Index frequently queried fields
- Use enums for fixed value sets
- Consider soft deletes via `deleted` boolean field

## Authentication & User Management
- Use established authentication patterns (Next-Auth, etc.)
- Follow existing user model structures
- Implement proper role-based access control
- Handle session management appropriately

## API & Server Components
- API routes: Use established session management
- Server Components: Use appropriate session handling
- Verify permissions before DB operations
- Return appropriate status codes
- Handle edge cases and errors gracefully

## Testing
- Use Jest with Prisma mocking capabilities
- Create realistic test fixtures
- Test role-based access where applicable
- Verify data isolation in multi-tenant scenarios
